THE SKIP HAS A PRICE, AND IT IS A MERGE-ORDER DEPENDENCY -- NOT A GUARD TO SILENCE.
Skipping 0316/0317 means that the moment our FIRST migration lands (0318, PR 17),
`check:migration-numbers` goes RED: "a NEW gap opened: 0315->0318". The guard is telling the
truth and its own message says why:

  "A new gap means a migration is expected to land LATER with a LOWER number. Production applies
   forward-only while CI rebuilds from a reset, so the two would then apply the same files in
   different orders -- and if the lower one depends on the higher one, a fresh reset simply fails."

That is EXACTLY our situation. origin/main is at 0314. We hold 0315 and 0318-0323; the other
campaign holds 0316/0317. Whichever of us merges second hands production a lower number after a
higher one.

